exports[`SpecService golden — loan-service renders deterministic SDD matching snapshot 1`] = `
"# loan-service — Software Design Document

> Stack: **java** · Architecture: **hexagonal** · Language: **en**
> Generated: 2026-05-04T00:00:00.000Z

Origination and underwriting platform

## 1. Executive Summary

**Problem.** Underwriting takes 3+ days; we want sub-5-minute decisions for prime applicants.

**Goals**

- Onboard 10k applicants in year-1
- Decision in <5 minutes for prime

**Key Performance Indicators**

- p95 decision latency < 5min
- Manual review rate < 20%

NARRATIVE


## 2. Stakeholders & Personas

| ID | Name | Role | Influence | Responsibilities |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| SH-001 | Lending CTO | sponsor | high | budget; scope |
| SH-002 | Risk officer | compliance | medium | policy |


## 3. Product Requirements

**Constraints**

- GDPR
- PCI-DSS

**Out of scope**

- No mobile app in v1
- No co-applicants in v1

### 3.1 Functional Requirements

#### FR-001 — Submit application

- **Priority:** must
- **Description:** Customer submits a loan application via web
- **Uses integrations:** INT-002

**Acceptance criteria**

- **AC-FR-001-1** — _Given_ an authenticated customer _When_ they submit a complete application _Then_ a record is persisted and INT-002 is queried

#### FR-002 — Auto-decision prime applicants

- **Priority:** must
- **Description:** Decisions for prime credit scores are automated
- **Uses integrations:** INT-001, INT-002

**Acceptance criteria**

- **AC-FR-002-1** — _Given_ a prime applicant _When_ the bureau returns a score _Then_ an approval is emitted to INT-001



## 4. Quality Attributes (NFR)

| ID | Category | Statement | Measurable target | Verification |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| NFR-001 | performance | Application API responds quickly | \`p95 < 200ms @ 100 RPS\` | — |
| NFR-002 | reliability | Service is highly available | \`99.9% uptime, RTO 15m, RPO 5m\` | — |

NARRATIVE


## 5. Glossary

| Term | Definition | Synonyms | Related |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Application** | A request for a loan | — | — |
| **Underwriting** | The risk assessment of an application | — | — |


## 6. System Architecture

> Architectural style: **hexagonal** · primary stack: **java**.

NARRATIVE

### 6.1 C4 Context (L1)

\`\`\`mermaid
C4Context
  title System Context — loan-service
  Person(user, "User", "Primary actor of the system")
  System(loan_service, "loan-service", "Origination and underwriting platform")
  Rel(user, loan_service, "uses")
  System_Ext(INT_001, "Camunda 8 (bpms)", "Loan origination workflow")
  Rel(loan_service, INT_001, "bpms")
  System_Ext(INT_002, "Bureau API (external-api)", "Credit lookup")
  Rel(loan_service, INT_002, "external-api")
  System_Ext(INT_003, "PostgreSQL (database)", "Application of record")
  Rel(loan_service, INT_003, "database")
\`\`\`

### 6.2 C4 Container (L2)

\`\`\`mermaid
C4Container
  Person(u, "User", "actor")
  Container(api, "API", "stack")
  Rel(u, api, "uses")
\`\`\`

### 6.3 C4 Component (L3)

\`\`\`mermaid
C4Component
  Component(svc, "Service", "core")
\`\`\`


## 7. Detailed Design

### 7.1 Domain Model

- **LoanApplication** _(context: Origination)_ — Aggregate root for an application
  - Entities: Application, Applicant
  - Value objects: Money
  - Events: ApplicationSubmitted, ApplicationApproved

\`\`\`mermaid
classDiagram
  class LoanApplication {
    +Application
    +Applicant
    -Money
  }
  class ApplicationSubmitted
  LoanApplication ..> ApplicationSubmitted : emits
  class ApplicationApproved
  LoanApplication ..> ApplicationApproved : emits
\`\`\`

### 7.2 Data Model

NARRATIVE

### 7.3 API Contracts

NARRATIVE

### 7.4 Integrations Catalog

| ID | Category | Name | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| INT-001 | bpms | Camunda 8 | Loan origination workflow |
| INT-002 | external-api | Bureau API | Credit lookup |
| INT-003 | database | PostgreSQL | Application of record |

> Full catalog: see [\`INTEGRATIONS.md\`](./INTEGRATIONS.md).

### 7.5 Workflow (BPMN)

\`\`\`mermaid
flowchart LR
  subgraph INT_001["Camunda 8"]
    INT_001_p_loanOrigination([loanOrigination])
    INT_001_t_scoreApplicant["scoreApplicant (service)"]
    INT_001_u_manualUnderwriting{{"manualUnderwriting (user)"}}
  end
\`\`\`

### 7.6 Key Sequence Diagrams

#### FR-001 — Submit application

\`\`\`mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  User->>Service: action
  Service-->>User: ok
\`\`\`

#### FR-002 — Auto-decision prime applicants

\`\`\`mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  User->>Service: action
  Service-->>User: ok
\`\`\`



## 8. Testing Strategy

NARRATIVE


## 9. Deployment & Operations

NARRATIVE

### 9.1 SLA / SLO / SLI

NARRATIVE

### 9.2 Observability Plan

NARRATIVE

### 9.3 Capacity & Scaling

NARRATIVE

### 9.4 Cost Model

NARRATIVE

### 9.5 Disaster Recovery

NARRATIVE

### 9.6 Migration & Rollback

NARRATIVE

### 9.7 Change Management

NARRATIVE


## 10. Implementation Plan

NARRATIVE


## 11. Architecture Decision Records

### ADR-001 — Use hexagonal architecture

- **Status:** \`accepted\` _(created 2026-05-04)_

**Context.** We need testable domain logic

**Decision.** Adopt ports and adapters

**Consequences.** Adapters must be thin

**Alternatives considered:** layered
**Related:** FR-001



## 12. Risks Register

| ID | Title | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation | Owner |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| RISK-001 | Bureau outage blocks underwriting | medium | high | Fallback to cached scores; circuit breaker | platform |


## 13. Compliance & Security

- PII encrypted at rest with KMS
- Audit log for every decision


## 14. Traceability Matrix

| Feature | Title | Acceptance Criteria | Integrations |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| FR-001 | Submit application | AC-FR-001-1 | INT-002 |
| FR-002 | Auto-decision prime applicants | AC-FR-002-1 | INT-001, INT-002 |

